td.p:
(l) to be loyal to their motherland, perform their functions and
                            responsibilities, maintain the security, honour and interests of their
                            motherland, and safeguard the security of Hong Kong;

dues or taxes on private immovable property
                            situated in the territory of China, excepting that used as the consular
                            premises;

estate, succession or inheritance duties, except
                            that movable property left in China by a deceased consular officer shall
                            be exempt therefrom;

“head of consular post” means the
                            consul-general, consul, vice-consul or consular agent charged by the
                            sending State with the duty of leading the consular post;

“consular officer” means the consul-general,
                            vice-consul-general, consul, vice-consul and consular attache or
                            consular agent;

“members of the service staff” mean the members
                            of the staff of the consular post engaged in the domestic service of the
                            consular post;

“members of the consular post” mean consular
                            officers, members of the administrative or technical staff of the
                            consular post and members of the service staff of the consular post;
